      "chapter": "Communications",
      "table_no": null,
      "title": "[Achievements of the five-year railway construction plan]",
      "caption_extra": "Among the more important achievements in connection with the five-year railway construction plan are the following :—",
      "continued": false,
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": null,
          "columns": [
            "No.",
            "Item"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "(1)",
              "The Chuchow-Kukong (Shaokwan) section of the Canton-Hankow Railway of 456 kilometers was opened to traffic in April, 1936 ;"
            ],
            [
              "(2)",
              "The Canton-Hankow and the Canton-Kowloon Railways were connected and through traffic began ten days after the war broke out ;"
            ],
            [
              "(3)",
              "Extension of the Lunghai Railway from Sian to Paoki (174 kilometers) before the war ;"
            ],
            [
              "(4)",
              "The Nanchang-Pinghsiang section of the Chekiang-Kiangsi Railway was rushed to completion and opened to traffic within a month's time after the war broke out ;"
            ],
            [
              "(5)",
              "Completion of the 75-kilometer Soochow-Kashing Railway ;"
            ],
            [
              "(6)",
              "Completion of the Hangchow-Tsaowokiang section and the bridge across the Chientang River ;"
            ],
            [
              "(7)",
              "Construction of the 365-kilometer Hengyang-Kweilin section of the Hunan-Kwangsi Railway at a speed of one kilometer a day. The work was begun three months after the war broke out and completed in October, 1938. A speed record in railway construction in China was thus set. (The previous records were an average of 12 days per kilom ter on the Peiping-Liaoning Railway and six days per kilometer on the Shanghai-Nanking Railway.)"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [],
      "transcriber_notes": [
        "Numbered list transcribed per the lists rule; 'kilom ter' printed so."
      ],
